# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

**/*.wasm

# Local experimental flow-graph frontend stack — gitignored until
# it stabilises and graduates from prototype.
crates/yel-flow-core/
crates/yel-flow-lsp/
crates/floc/
yel-flow-editor/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# LLVM coverage instrumentation artifacts
*.profraw

# Rewrite oracle corpus — the 8000 ARTIFACT BODIES are local-only (2026-07-30).
#
# 209 MB, previously tracked via git-lfs. Removed from history: the LFS batch
# API rate-limits a first-time 8000-object upload, and 8000 entries make every
# PR diff unreviewable.
#
# The four artifact directories are ignored; `corpus/`'s plain-text metadata is
# NOT — SHA256SUMS, MANIFEST and known-failures.txt total 617 KB (0.3% of the
# corpus) and are the whole point of keeping anything: `shasum -c` still answers
# "did anything move?" over all 8000 files, and MANIFEST still pins the freeze
# SHA. Losing the bodies costs you the ability to *diff* a divergence; losing
# these would cost you the ability to *detect* one.
#
# Regenerate bodies with scripts/freeze-corpus.sh at the freeze SHA. Read
# plans/rewrite/corpus.md first — seed N does NOT reproduce the same program
# across yel-smith versions, so a regenerated corpus is a DIFFERENT corpus
# unless the freeze SHA matches.
corpus/src/
corpus/wit/
corpus/dot/
corpus/wasm/

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store
